(Hi Mojtaba,) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (I'll try to be more clear.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Q: in total what does the BIASIN pin do and whats it's role?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (A: In the event that the BIAS electrode becomes disconnected from the patient,) Tj
T* (by having BIASOUT connected to BIASIIN, the BIASOUT signal can be routed through) Tj
T* (BIASIN and back to the patient through one of the input electrodes. This way, the patient) Tj
T* (stays biased and the measurements stay within the common-mode input range of the PGA.) Tj
T* (Of course, one measurement will be "lost" since it's being used to bias the patient.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Q: it should be done in both cascade or daisy chain mode or it's just for daisy chain?) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (A: it's the same for both modes.) Tj
